error[ffi_tag_is_a_union]: `fixedbugs-157-unions.h` declares `utag` as a `union`, not a struct — C keeps the two in one namespace and will not let one stand for the other
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-157-a-handle-over-a-union-s-tag.hero:17:19
     |
  17 |     record UH tag utag  #~ ffi_tag_is_a_union
     |                   ^^^^
  note: a `tag` names a struct (§4.19), and a handle reaches a union by a typedef's name. If `fixedbugs-157-unions.h` gives `utag` a typedef, write that name after `tag`; if not, give it one in a header of the program's own, `typedef union utag UH_t;`, and write `record UH tag UH_t`, or pass it to C as a `ptr`
